---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About — Trump Account Guide"
  description="An independent guide that makes the $1,000 Trump Account benefit easy to understand for every family."
  locale="en"
>
  <section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-xl px-4 py-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-black text-slate-900">About this site</h1>

    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
      <p>
        The Trump Account is a brand-new federal program. Babies born between 2025 and 2028 get
        <strong>$1,000</strong> from the government, automatically — there is no income limit and
        no complicated application.
      </p>
      <p>
        Almost every other site explaining this program is built for high-income families who
        already understand investing. This one is built for everyone else: parents who hear about
        the $1,000 from a friend, on TikTok, or from a community worker, and just want to know two
        things in plain language —
      </p>
      <ul class="ml-6 list-disc space-y-1">
        <li>Does my kid get the money?</li>
        <li>How much could it grow into?</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can answer both in under a minute, with nothing more than your child's birth year and
        an honest guess of what you can set aside each day. We don't ask for your name, your
        email, or your SSN — and we never will.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is an <strong>independent</strong> educational resource. It is not affiliated
        with the U.S. government, with any financial institution, or with any political campaign.
        To actually open an account, visit
        <a href="https://trumpaccounts.gov" class="text-brand-green-dark underline" rel="noopener">
          trumpaccounts.gov
        </a>
        on or after July 4, 2026.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border-2 border-slate-100 bg-white p-5">
      <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">
        How we calculate
      </div>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-700">
        We run a 1,000-path Monte Carlo simulation over the historical S&P 500 monthly return
        distribution (1985–2026), with 12 monthly draws per year compounded multiplicatively. The
        gross historical mean is reduced by a 0.10%/yr fund expense ratio (typical for a low-cost
        S&P 500 index ETF), giving an effective ≈10.5% annualized return; the headline is the
        median across the 1,000 paths. Contributions are clamped at the federal $5,000/yr §530A
        cap, and the $1,000 pilot seed is added when the child's birth year is 2025–2028. Returns
        in any individual case can be substantially higher or lower than the median — including
        losses.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
